= Complex Semisimple Lie Groups <ch:complex-semisimple-lie-groups>

#source(151)This chapter deals with the most explored section of the theory of
Lie groups and Lie algebras. Its main result is the complete classification of
connected complex semisimple Lie groups and their irreducible linear
representations. This classification is based on the theory of root systems,
which because of its numerous applications deserves a special treatment. The
theory is axiomatically developed in §~@sec:root-systems. During the whole
chapter (except
@ss:invariant-scalar-products[°]--@ss:normal-subgroups-of-semisimple[°]) the
ground field is $CC$. All the vector spaces and Lie algebras considered are
finite-dimensional.
